  "notes": "Image 1 = C-language names (port names used as labels), image 2 = Arduino pin numbers (used as labels); board silkscreen (B0, D5, ...) is first in functions. Overlined signal names are written with a \"~\" prefix (~OC4A, ~OC4B, ~OC4D). Corner pads belong to the side columns; the bottom row lists the 5 pads between them, mapped via drawn leader lines for PD5/PD4 (23/22). Interior PE6/24 and AREF pads are grouped as one horizontal pair. Skipped: mini-USB, pushbutton."
